description:
fz's Enum extremes (lib/enum.fz) cover what the distiller needs: max/1,2 and min/1,2 with a zero-arity empty_fallback, max_by/2, min_by/2, min_max/1, min_max_by/2, over lists only. Elixir 1.20.4 (../elixir lib/elixir/lib/enum.ex:1865-2370) offers more:

- any enumerable (`@spec max(t, ...)`); fz's specs say `[a]`, so `Enum.max(1..4)` is rejected at compile time;
- max/2, min/2 whose second argument is a 2-arity sorter (`&>=/2`) or a module compared via `module.compare/2`, told apart from a fallback with `is_function(f, 0)` / `is_function(f, 2)`;
- max/3, min/3 (sorter and fallback); max_by/3,4, min_by/3,4; min_max/2,3; min_max_by/3,4.

Elixir keeps the first of equal elements (default sorter >= / <=); fz already does.

Each form gets checked against an Elixir oracle on interp, run and build. Blocked by is_function/1,2 and by module names as values. Not needed by the distiller.
